Fix the OpenGL test data generator sample of OpenCV 5.0.0

loadMesh() and the triangle rasterization API moved to the ptcloud module in OpenCV 5,
but the sample still only includes/links geometry, so building the examples
(-DBUILD_EXAMPLES=ON with OpenGL) fails with "'loadMesh' was not declared in this scope".

--- a/samples/opengl/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/samples/opengl/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
   opencv_imgproc
   opencv_imgcodecs
   opencv_geometry
+  opencv_ptcloud
   opencv_videoio
   opencv_highgui)
 ocv_check_dependencies(${OPENCV_OPENGL_SAMPLES_REQUIRED_DEPS})
--- a/samples/opengl/opengl_testdata_generator.cpp
+++ b/samples/opengl/opengl_testdata_generator.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "opencv2/imgproc.hpp"
 #include "opencv2/highgui.hpp"
 #include "opencv2/geometry.hpp"
+#include "opencv2/ptcloud.hpp"

 using namespace std;
 using namespace cv;
